{
  "name": "compensation reaches no hirer, on any surface, before or after acceptance",
  "description": "ADR-0018 §2, the decision the whole feature turns on: A HIRER NEVER SEES EXPECTED COMPENSATION. Not on a scorecard, not on a contact request, not after an acceptance, not ever.\n\nIt is a NEGATIVE, and a negative is what review is worst at. So this case leans on the runner deliberately rather than incidentally: Compare fails on a key present in the response but absent from the snapshot, which means every recorded body below ASSERTS THE ABSENCE of currency, hourly_rate and yearly_amount by not mentioning them. If an implementation ever adds the figure to any of these shapes, that step fails — no assertion has to be written for a field nobody has thought of yet, which is the only form of this test that survives the API growing.\n\nThe hirer-facing bodies are copied verbatim from the approved discovery fixtures for the same reason: what is under test is that stating a salary expectation changes NOTHING a hirer receives, and a retyped body would quietly be asserting something else.\n\nSeven surfaces, reached by a VERIFIED hirer — the account with the most capability the platform grants: search results, the scorecard, a shortlist entry, the shortlist read, a contact request before acceptance, the same request after acceptance, the leaderboard, and the public scorecard. Plus /me, plus the refusal of /me/compensation to a hirer, which is the statement that no hirer route to the figure exists at all rather than one that returns nothing.\n\nDecision 3 is the reason the after-acceptance step matters most: compensation filters the CONTRIBUTOR's view of roles and never the hirer's view of people, because a hirer who knows what you will accept offers exactly that, and an expectation stops being a floor and becomes a ceiling.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories", "scored_population"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "Alice states what she expects to be paid. Everything after this step is a check that no hirer can reach it — so this step is the one that makes the rest meaningful, and the db assertion proves the figure really is stored rather than quietly dropped.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/me/compensation",
        "body": {
          "currency": "GBP",
          "hourly_rate": 4500,
          "yearly_amount": 9500000
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "currency": "GBP",
          "hourly_rate": 4500,
          "yearly_amount": 9500000
        },
        "db": {
          "user_compensation": {
            "where": {
              "user_id": "{{alice.id}}"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "currency": "GBP",
              "hourly_rate": 4500,
              "yearly_amount": 9500000
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "THE ONLY READ THAT EVER RETURNS THE FIGURE, and it belongs to the person who typed it — ADR-0018 §Compensation.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/compensation"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "currency": "GBP",
          "hourly_rate": 4500,
          "yearly_amount": 9500000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Work preferences are a SEPARATE pair from compensation (ADR-0018 §11), so the profile a contributor edits most often carries no salary and the profile read below does not incidentally return one.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/me/profile",
        "body": {
          "open_to_remote": true,
          "open_to_internships": false,
          "open_to_onsite": false,
          "open_to_contract": true,
          "open_to_freelance": false,
          "current_country": "GB",
          "office_yoe": 6,
          "first_pr_url": "https://github.com/indie/smalllib/pull/12",
          "latest_pr_url": "https://github.com/acme/platform/pull/56"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "preferences": {
            "open_to_remote": true,
            "open_to_internships": false,
            "open_to_onsite": false,
            "open_to_contract": true,
            "open_to_freelance": false,
            "current_country": "GB",
            "office_yoe": 6,
            "first_pr_url": "https://github.com/indie/smalllib/pull/12",
            "latest_pr_url": "https://github.com/acme/platform/pull/56"
          },
          "availability": {
            "status": "looking",
            "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
          },
          "needs_attention": false,
          "readiness": {
            "findable": true,
            "blocking": [],
            "limiting": []
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "There is no hirer route to the figure, not even the contributor's own one. A verified hirer asking for it is refused on the type of their account, before any lookup happens.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/compensation"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "contributor_required"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The contributor's own /me. Compensation is absent here too: it travels on one endpoint, not on whatever the profile screen happened to already be fetching.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
          "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
          "github_login": "aliceok",
          "email": "alice@example.com",
          "principal_type": "contributor",
          "availability": {
            "status": "looking",
            "expires_at": "<timestamp>"
          },
          "overall_score": 64.2,
          "generalist_score": 64.2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "AND NO ROUTE TO SOMEBODY ELSE'S. Decision 2 says there is no endpoint that carries it, which is a statement about the ROUTING TABLE and not about a response body — so it is asserted where a route would have to appear. A 404 here is the absence itself; the day somebody adds a hirer-facing read this step answers 200 and fails, which no assertion about a field could do.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/contributors/{{alice.id}}/compensation"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 404
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "And nobody at all is refused before the type check, not after it.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/compensation"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 401,
        "body": {
          "error": "unauthenticated"
        }
      }
    },
